    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n103089" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τέος</span></b>  and <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τεός</span></b> , 
			Ion.
		 and 
			Dor.
		 for <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τίς, τις</span>, rare in nom.
		and acc., <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οὔτε γὰρ οὔ τεον ἔστι</span>
		nor is there a No<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>thing</i>,
				<i><span class="en">
				Parm.
				8.46
			</span></i>; but some of the oblique cases occur in <i><span class="en">
				Hdt.
			</span></i>, etc., 
				v.
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τέῳ, τέων, τέοισι;
				τεοις</span>
			
			<i><span class="en">
				Xenoph.
				37
			</span></i>; cf. also <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τέο</span>.</div>
